Well, ImageMagick uses a large number of libraries that are already
present on a decent Linux installation.  Windows doesn't have them (in
other words, it does things sufficiently different so that a Linux-based
tool can't switch easily), so they must be included with the
installation, which explains that difference.  Linux has those libraries
in other packages that don't count for IM download size…


